{# magic-link.v1 — TRANSACTIONAL sign-in link (#2272).
   payload = { link, expires_minutes }

   Three ways this message differs from every other template here, each deliberate:

   1. NO UNSUBSCRIBE FOOTER. Every notification template ends with one; this must not. You cannot
      unsubscribe from being able to log in, and an auth envelope carries no `consent_snapshot` and
      therefore no `unsubscribe_ref` — so a footer here would render a dead link into a real inbox.
   2. NO GRAPH CHIPS. The other templates carry corpus content and the moat rule applies to them.
      This message is about the recipient's own session, not about the corpus.
   3. ONE ACTION, AND IT IS A SECRET. The link is the credential while it lives. The copy says how
      long that is, and says plainly what to do if they did not ask for it — because an unexpected
      sign-in email is the one signal a person gets that someone typed their address.

   Everything else follows the standard shell (your-week-digest.v1): the same wrapper table, the
   same <h1> and subtitle, the same palette. The button uses the shell's chip/border colour
   #1e2739 with light text; the first version had a light pill with dark text that appeared in no
   other email.

   Every text block sits in a table cell with the colour set on the CELL as well as the text. The
   fallback-link line was a bare <p> and showed near-black on the dark card in Gmail (iOS) in
   later messages of a thread, while the identically coloured footer, already in a coloured cell,
   stayed readable (2026-10-03). The cause inside Gmail is not verified; this removes the one
   structural difference between the line that broke and the lines that did not. #}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"></head>
<body style="margin:0;padding:0;background-color:#080d1b;">
<table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" bgcolor="#080d1b" style="background-color:#080d1b;">
  <tr><td align="center" style="padding:32px 16px;">
    <table role="presentation" width="600" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" bgcolor="#080d1b" style="width:600px;max-width:600px;background-color:#080d1b;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;">
      <tr><td style="padding:0 8px;">
        {% include "email/_brand.html.j2" %}
        <h1 style="font-size:24px;font-weight:600;margin:8px 0 4px;color:#f0eae0;">Sign in to Close Listening</h1>
        <div style="font-size:14px;color:#acb2c2;margin:0 0 20px;">Tap the button below and you are in. No password to remember.</div>

        {# A table so Outlook renders the button; the plain link below is the fallback. #}
        <table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="margin:0 0 20px;">
          <tr><td bgcolor="#efa843" style="background-color:#efa843;border-radius:6px;">
            <a href="{{ payload.link }}" style="display:inline-block;padding:11px 24px;font-size:15px;font-weight:700;color:#080d1b;text-decoration:none;border-radius:6px;">Sign in</a>
          </td></tr>
        </table>

        <table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="border-top:1px solid #1e2739;"><tr><td style="padding:18px 0;color:#acb2c2;font-size:13px;line-height:1.5;">
          <p style="margin:0 0 10px;color:#acb2c2;">This link works once and expires in {{ payload.expires_minutes | default(15) }} minutes.</p>
          <p style="margin:0 0 4px;color:#acb2c2;">If the button does not work, paste this into your browser:</p>
          <a href="{{ payload.link }}" style="color:#acb2c2;word-break:break-all;">{{ payload.link }}</a>
        </td></tr></table>

        {% set footer_reason %}You are receiving this because someone asked to sign in with this address. If that was not you, ignore this email — the link expires on its own and nothing happens.{% endset %}
        {% include "email/_footer.html.j2" %}
      </td></tr>
    </table>
  </td></tr>
</table>
</body>
</html>
